 "title": "Think about farming when it rains",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator advises against settling for shallow goals when life is going well, arguing instead to capitalize on your momentum. By drawing on a quote about focusing on farming rather than romance during the rain, she explains that successful people constantly double down on their efforts while they have their health and capability.",
 "key_points": [
  "When things are going well, people often focus on shallow goals like going on dates, fancy cafes, or trips.",
  "Successful top 1 percent earners constantly want to double down on the revenue they are making.",
  "The creator highlights the advantage of the moment: having the job, money, health, and mental capability right now.",
  "The creator advises: \"When it's raining in your life, when things are going good, do not think about romance, think about what you should do next.\""
 ],
 "content": "The creator shares a tweet on screen: \"You are poor because when it rains, you think about romance instead of farming.\" She explains that when you still have your job, money, health, and mental capability, you should avoid focusing on shallow goals like going on dates, fancy cafes, or trips. She notes that people in her network who are in the top 1% are always looking to double down on their revenue. She explains that they realize the advantage of the present moment, knowing they have the health and mental capacity to keep going today, whereas tomorrow they might not. Her final advice is that when things are going well in your life, you should not focus on romance; instead, you should focus on your next steps.",
